<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cingetorix (Treveri)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1st century BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cingetorix-cantium">Cingetorix</a> was a noble of the Treveri, a Gallic people of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moselle">Moselle</a> valley, in the 50s BCE. He backed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a> against his father-in-law <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indutiomarus">Indutiomarus</a>, leader of the anti-Roman faction, and Caesar recognised him as chief of the tribe in 54 BCE. Indutiomarus declared him a public enemy and seized his property before being killed in 53 BCE.</p></div>
